WEBVTT

00:00:45.274 --> 00:00:47.580
We're under attack! Evasive action!

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.170
We're not under attack.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.880
I was trying to tilt my seat back,

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.970
and instead, the ship went
into catastrophe mode.

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.630
Activating sprinklers!

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:59.680
Hellballs! The wires are all crossed!

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.560
Uh-oh! Can opener!

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:07.150
Down in the valley

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.230
More hellballs!

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.320
Hang your head over...

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:12.650
Ow!

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.950
I'll get you, can opener,
if it's the last thing I ever--

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:24.910
Do you hear something?

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:27.170
Sounds like a screaming
coming across the sky.

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:32.050
Ah, that explains it.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:35.470
Should we check for survivors?
- After a crash like that?

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:38.050
What's the point?

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:49.860
Thank God the can opener
had the presence of mind

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.270
to cut an escape hole.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:52.770
It's a hero!

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:55.110
I coulda bent us an escape hole.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:58.450
But did anybody ask Bender? No!

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:01.870
- Are you alright?
- No, I'm not alright!

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:03.660
I was talking to the can opener.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.830
What about you? Are you alright?

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:08.290
No! I was nearly smushed!

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:10.330
I was talking to the ship!

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:14.920
Poor old Bessie.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:17.130
I'm afraid her time has come.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:20.720
Why did it have to be her instead of me?!

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.100
Hello? Gaping head wound!

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:47.370
There it is. The Graveyard of Ships.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:49.540
The plasma sea

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.880
at the bottom of the multiverse.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:55.590
Mariners call it the Tropic of Ghosts.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:59.090
They're pretty stupid, though.
- I'd hate to be here at night.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:01.890
- It is night.
- Then I hate being here!

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:09.890
I built that ship
with my own two hands,

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:13.310
as well as several hundred
high-powered hydraulic hands.

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:17.280
Did I ever tell you about
all the different lengths of wire I used?

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.530
Yes!

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:21.820
She saw us through
lots of great adventures.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:24.200
And a few mediocre ones.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.790
Honestly, some of those
three-part adventures were kinda sloppy.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:31.000
We had a nice run,
but nothing lasts forever.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.580
Except me, apparently.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:37.090
Hey, what are those shmierd currents
under the surface?

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:40.470
Merely jet streams
of alternate realities.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:43.590
All that is, was, or might have been.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.680
And a lot of other crap, too.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:49.180
Alternate realities
can bite my shiny metal ass!

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.600
Bender! Show some ass respect!

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.230
Hiya!
- Ha, ha! You missed!

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:58.230
- Hiya!
- Oof!

00:03:58.230 --> 00:03:59.530
Not in that reality.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.660
dissonant note

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:07.870
My heartfelt symphonies.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.200
Oh, lord.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.080
When a vessel so renowned

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:13.870
as the Planet Express ship
is laid to rest,

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:16.670
it's only fitting that
the DOOP's greatest hero

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.670
say a few words in tribute.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:21.050
Or better yet, sing them!

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:27.010
That ship is like a ship on the ocean

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:32.850
It's been sailing with a cargo
full of love and devotion

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:34.310
So, rock the boat

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:35.350
Come on, Kif.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:37.440
Don't rock the boat, baby.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:38.820
Rock the boat

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.940
Don't tip the boat over

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.280
Thank you.
Check out our SoundCloud.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:45.570
I see by the clock-ometer,

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:48.910
there's still a few minutes
before the scuttling charges detonate

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:50.910
and sink your ship forever.

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:53.710
So, if you'd like to pay
your final respects...

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:57.380
Yes. Let's view its spacely remains.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:08.680
This ship was my first home
when I came to the future.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.770
I slept right here
on this stained carpeting.

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:14.770
- You're what stained it!
- Remember this table?

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:18.360
I had a meal there. Once.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:22.230
Ugh! How can you meatbags
get so weepy about a ship?

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:23.820
It's just a hunk of tin!

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:26.410
You're 40% tin!

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:29.530
And didn't you once have
a torrid affair with this ship?

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:31.870
I have torrid affairs
with lots of things.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.330
Then I move on.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.710
Bender don't look back!

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:37.170
'Cause his neck joint don't turn that way!

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.170
Ooh, snap!

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:41.630
Doo dat doodle-oo deedle-ee boo

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:55.520
So many memories.

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:01.980
Ah! Too many memories!

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:11.870
Eh, whatever. Let's go.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:13.120
Move it along, Leela!

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.370
The explosives are set
to go off in 15 minutes.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.000
Wait, where's Fry?

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.080
How should I know?
You're his mother.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:22.790
Oops, sorry. I meant 15 seconds.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:25.050
What?! Quick, we've got to find Fry!

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:31.050
Come back! There's no time!

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.720
- Leela!
- Amy!

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:34.260
Dr. Zoidberg!

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.520
So, uh...

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:45.570
this graveyard need a janitor?

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.500
- Fry...
- Leela?

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.330
Why is... me?

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:02.580
He's okay!
His pulse is steady as an abalone!

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:04.460
What happened?

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:06.760
We were all on the ship when it sank.

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:09.050
We nearly drowned trying to save you!

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:12.590
I swallowed a lot of
quasi-neutral plasma.

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:17.310
Why didn't you come out sooner,
you boob?

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:19.020
I had some kind of attack.

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:21.440
I started seeing flashes
of things that happened.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.110
Also, things that didn't happen.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:26.320
Except it felt like they did happen.
Or will happen!

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.280
Well, these things happen.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.320
Or don't. Or will. Or...

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:31.910
Let's just go.

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:38.660
Leela, you and I could've died
on that ship.

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:41.920
- True so far.
- But then, we'd never have gotten...

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:43.130
Never have gotten what?

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:45.840
Uh, the tattoos with each other's names.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.000
I already have one.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.460
I used to date a different guy named Fry.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:51.340
Then, how come I've never seen it?

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:53.300
It's in a very out-of-the-way spot.

00:07:57.850 --> 00:08:00.020
Whoa! Someone's all duded up!

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:02.770
Bender, life can go
in a lot of directions.

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:04.060
Up, left,

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:05.310
community college,

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:08.780
but I know exactly which direction
I want mine to go.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:10.360
So tonight, at sunset,

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:13.530
I'm meeting Leela on top of
the Vampire State Building.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:15.410
I'm gonna ask her to marry me.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:17.990
When I said someone's all duded up,
I meant me.

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:19.620
Check out the Rolex.

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:21.710
I bent it off a guy I know.

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:23.000
By the way, you're late.

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:32.720
- Big night, eh, Mr. Fry?
- The biggest, Janös!

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:34.590
I'm gonna ask Leela to marry me!

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:36.550
Leela? Bluh!

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:39.720
My gosh. This is incredible!

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:42.230
I feel like I died and went to here.

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:44.230
But luckily, you didn't.

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:47.310
A toast. I...

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:49.690
I...
- What's the matter?

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:51.400
Nothing. I-I just felt strange,

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:53.820
like we'd had champagne here before.

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:57.120
Janös has served many before you.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:58.910
Their souls linger

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:02.700
long after the champagne has been drunk...

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:04.580
Yeah, that's probably it.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:08.130
Anyhow, Leela, I brought you here
to ask you something.

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:10.840
Ooh! Lookie there!

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:16.090
- What is it?
- This ring!

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:18.510
Th-The table! The plain white napkins!

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:20.430
I'm sure I've done this before!

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:23.310
Fry, I'd remember a ring like this.

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:25.140
Woo!

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:27.600
Janös, you remember
this happening, don't you?

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:31.480
It is a curse of my kind
to remember everything.

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:34.490
Oh, I forgot your hors d'oeuvres.

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:38.660
It's like I'm having a dream,
except I'm not having a dream.

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:41.870
It's more like watching a movie
when I'm half asleep.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:44.120
Oh, you're having an Avatar?

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:54.090
Fry! What's wrong?

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:57.470
I don't know. I'm seeing you,
but I'm seeing other stuff, too.

00:09:57.470 --> 00:10:01.180
Me! You! Plain white napkins!

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:02.890
Look out! The railing!

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:09.980
Janös, quick!
Help me get him to a doctor!

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:16.320
You know, he'd be a lot easier to handle

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:18.820
if he had less blood.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:19.910
Just saying.

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:27.080
Well, your head seems normal,

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:29.500
aside from that weird face on the front.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:31.040
So what happened this time?

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:32.750
It was just like on the ship.

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:34.880
I felt like everything's happened before,

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:37.880
even things that didn't happen yet!
Does that make sense?

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:39.640
No! You're a terrible patient!

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:42.680
Could Fry be seeing
some kind of alternate universe?

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:43.890
Or a time loop?

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:46.600
Nonsense.
Those things are completely possible

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:47.980
and happen all the time,

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:51.360
but this sounds like
a textbook case of déjà vu.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.480
Déjà vu?
I feel like I've heard of that before.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:57.110
No, wait.
I'm thinking of De La Soul.

00:10:57.110 --> 00:10:58.780
You have all the symptoms.

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:02.490
The feeling you are experiencing something
that's already happened?

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:03.870
That's all the symptoms.

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:05.410
It's not déjà vu!

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:07.870
I'm sure the things I'm seeing
are real somehow.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:10.080
You don't think I'm crazy, do you, Leela?

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:12.130
I... don't know what to think.

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:15.170
I love you so much,

00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:17.710
and all I ever wanted to do is marry you.

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:21.260
But first, I need to understand
what's happening to me.

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:23.050
I'm not going anywhere.

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:25.100
No one's not going anywhere!

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:27.270
Because everyone's going to the hangar

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:30.560
to see the new ship I just completed.

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:40.950
Okay, already, we see it!

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:43.200
Pretty cool, eh?

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:45.950
It's got cutting-edge
artificial intelligence.

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:47.490
And to provide its speech,

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:50.830
I hired the world's greatest voice actor,

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:52.500
Tress LaMarche!

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:53.500
Hi, there.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:56.300
It's even got a new
cloaking device I invented!

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:58.340
Plus an uncloaking device.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:00.550
And a cloak room!

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:02.550
It's like living in the future!

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:05.800
Oh my, yes!
You should see the wire I used.

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:07.930
All the latest lengths!

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:11.190
Now, this is comfy.

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:13.520
Do I feel an electric seat warmer?

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:16.320
You do! The AI automatically adjusts

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:18.360
to ambient butt temperature.

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:21.200
Wow. Hear that, Fry?

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:22.860
Yeah. Sounds great.

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:24.410
I thought you'd be excited.

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:27.120
You're always complaining
about my chronic cold butt.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:30.040
It's just, I miss the old ship.

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:33.460
I feel like maybe something important
was on it when it sank.

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:37.210
This ship's nice, but it feels... wrong.

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:39.590
Well, I'm just happy it
doesn't have a can opener.

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:41.800
That's where you're not happy, Bender.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:45.590
The one thing I saved from
the old ship was the can opener!

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:48.180
It even has its own sleeping quarters.

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:53.270
What?! Where's my sleeping quarters?!

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:54.520
You don't need any!

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:57.770
This ship is so fast,
you won't have time to rest.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:13:00.400
That's just a perk for heroes.

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:04.860
sinister crescendo

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:14.120
Cheer up, guys.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:16.540
At least we get to go
to a tropical paradise

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.250
for our first delivery.

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:33.350
Woo! That was exhausting.

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:36.100
- No, it wasn't.
- Yes, it was.

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:37.980
I need a nap. And for that,

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:39.690
I'll need sleeping quarters!

00:13:40.940 --> 00:13:42.150
Get out.

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:45.200
Bender, no! That can opener

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:47.740
is the finest swordsman in all of space!

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:48.660
Eh?

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:52.080
Oh, yeah?

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:58.830
You shot a guy who only had a sword?!

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:01.420
What? I saw it in a movie.
It was hilarious.

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:03.760
You think they'll try me as an adult?
- I would.

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:06.220
Wake up, Canny!

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:08.470
Please!

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:09.470
Wake up!

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:12.850
It's over, buddy.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:15.640
How can I go on?

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:17.310
My nemesis is dead!

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:20.020
I'm like Superman without Lex Luthor!

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:22.230
Aquaman without that big old shrimp!

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:24.280
Ow.

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:26.570
You want your hand and your Rolex?

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:28.910
No. I shall go on without them

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:30.910
in tribute to a worthy foe

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:33.660
who met his match in Bender One-Hand.

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:35.580
That's what you have
to call me from now on.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:37.410
Bender One-Hand!

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:39.710
Or Bender No-Watch!

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:41.540
Nah, I might get a watch
for my other hand.

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:43.590
Anyway, I still need that nap.

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:47.380
Ahh...

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:53.510
Vessel ahead.

00:14:53.510 --> 00:14:55.890
Vessel ahead.
- That's weird.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.890
Something's showing up on radar,

00:14:57.890 --> 00:14:59.480
but I don't see anything.

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:03.070
What? What is it, boy?

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:04.860
The old Planet Express ship!

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:06.360
See it?

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:07.570
I don't see squat.

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:10.570
I-It's right there,
next to the space stuff.

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:15.910
Fry, a little psychotic break
with reality is perfectly normal.

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:19.040
Sometimes, I think I can control
the weather.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:21.710
It flew away.

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:23.880
Butt warmer engaged.

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:25.340
Ahh...

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:27.880
I wish we'd never scuttled the old ship.

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:30.510
This new ship just can't replace it.

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:33.260
You know,
I can hear everything you're saying.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:39.390
And in tonight's
"News of the Supernatural,"

00:15:39.390 --> 00:15:42.060
ghost ships.

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:47.690
This whole segment
is beneath Morbo's journalistic dignity!

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:51.200
Captain Brannigan,
what's all this nonsense about...

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.620
ghost ships?

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:55.700
Well, Linda, sensors have detected

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:57.870
a phantom vessel in this quadrant,

00:15:57.870 --> 00:16:00.040
but it's invisible to the nude eye.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:03.460
We suspect pirates have
salvaged an abandoned vessel

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:06.300
and equipped it with cloaking technology.

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:08.800
But, if it is ghosts, rest assured,

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:12.180
Zapp Brannigan will blast
them out of existence!

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:13.640
Or back into it, I guess.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:17.010
I saw that ghost ship!
It's our old ship!

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:19.390
But, nobody besides you is seeing it.

00:16:19.390 --> 00:16:22.390
Explain that with your precious science.

00:16:22.390 --> 00:16:25.440
I can't.
Look, I don't know how or why...

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:26.940
Oh, there's a first.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:29.690
...but something important
went down with that ship.

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:33.110
Please, can we go back
and see if it's still where we sank it?

00:16:34.110 --> 00:16:37.530
Well, I guess it couldn't hurt
to take another look.

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:39.700
Come on, Bender.
- Ah-ah-ah.

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:42.000
Bender One-Hand.

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:54.590
We're approaching
the Graveyard of Ships.

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:57.050
Ooh...

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:03.480
Attention, unknown vessel.

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:07.310
Oh! Hello, Leela.
That's a hot new ship you're wearing.

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:10.480
Spare me the whatever that was.
What do you want?

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:13.360
An invisible ship's been
reported in this quadrant,

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:17.120
and my orders are to see
no one goes in or out.

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:20.290
Or not see them, if they're invisible.
Understood?

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:21.580
Understood.

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:22.960
Aw...

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:24.250
And ignored.

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:30.380
Oh, no, you doo-n't.

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:32.880
Kif, set course for follow that ship.

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:44.100
Cloaking device activated.

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:47.520
But, the graveyard's locked up.
How are we gonna get in there?

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:49.440
Pure dumb brute force.

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:51.150
Cloaking device, eh?

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:54.900
Kif, activate our cloaking device.
And spare me your,

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:56.860
"Eh, we don't have one."

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:03.500
Um, sir, the graveyard's locked up.

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:05.290
How are we going to get in there?

00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:07.710
Kif, we're invisible now, remember?

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:10.790
We'll simply pass right through the gate.

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:12.670
Being invisible doesn't-- Oh jeez.

00:18:16.220 --> 00:18:18.140
It's open! Full speed ahead!

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:20.220
But it's dark in there,

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:21.930
and full of dead spaceships!

00:18:21.930 --> 00:18:23.220
I said go!

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:37.910
Okay, that's where our old ship sank.

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:40.570
But I see little, if any, wreckage.

00:18:40.570 --> 00:18:43.740
That proves it became a ghost
and started haunting me.

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:46.160
There's no other rational explanation.

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:50.670
There are 38,651
other rational explanations.

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:55.630
Keep your eyes peeled for anything
that looks remotely invisible.

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:59.260
Incoming fire from that
empty spot over there, sir!

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:02.180
Playing hard to see, eh, Leela?

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:03.430
Return fire!

00:19:03.430 --> 00:19:05.770
Someone's firing at us!

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:07.140
And missing badly.

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:10.150
Sounds like Zapp. Return fire!

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:11.560
- Firing!
- Firing!

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:13.440
- Fire more!
- Fire harder!

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:24.540
Yes! We hit the Nimbus!

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:30.920
Uh-oh. We destroyed the Nimbus.

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:32.960
Look! An escape pod!

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:34.880
Ah, crap. Survivors.

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:37.760
We are in big trouble!

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:40.010
Uh... Here, Bender.

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:41.840
Sit in the captain's chair.

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:45.060
Butt warmer destroyed.

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:48.560
Attention, Leela, wherever you are.

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:50.440
We victoriously surrender

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:53.480
and triumphantly beg to come aboard.

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:56.440
De-cloak the ship.

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:05.910
You win this round, Captain Leela,

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:09.000
but when the DOOP finds out
you destroyed the Nimbus--

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:11.620
It wasn't me. It was Captain Bender.

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:12.710
Nuh-uh!

00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:14.880
Captain Bender One-Hand!

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:16.840
See? Look at that. Nothing.

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:20.050
Hey, someone's still firing!

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:21.720
Another invisible ship?

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:25.640
It's the ghost ship!
Let's get outta here!

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:29.220
No, Leela! Running away from ghosts
only encourages them.

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:32.350
It's the classic Jerry Lewis mistake.

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:33.730
I'm taking command.

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:36.860
Oh no, you aren't.
I'm captain of this ship.

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:38.320
Put up your...

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:41.110
Oh... Right. Carry on, Captain.

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:47.450
There's only one way
to hit an enemy you can't see.

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:49.490
Fire an infinite number of missiles

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:51.660
in all possible directions.

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:54.080
But we have less than
an infinite number left.

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:55.170
We have zero.

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:56.960
Then we'll have to improvise.

00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:58.800
Fire all the escape pods!

00:21:03.380 --> 00:21:06.010
Hull breach imminent.

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:08.010
Quick! To the escape pods!

00:21:10.350 --> 00:21:12.430
I guess this is the end again.

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:15.690
I don't mind dying,
as long as it's with you.

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:18.230
I'm just sorry we never
got a chance to be married.

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:20.230
Me, too.

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:23.240
Wait! A ship's captain can marry people!

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:24.490
Please?

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:25.820
Captain?

00:21:25.820 --> 00:21:29.660
But Leela, I always hoped that we...

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:30.660
We what?

00:21:30.660 --> 00:21:32.450
Nothing.

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:35.080
I shall be happy to perform the ceremony.

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:40.050
Do you, Fry,

00:21:40.050 --> 00:21:42.670
a delivery boy, for God's sake,

00:21:42.670 --> 00:21:44.300
take Leela to be your wife?

00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:46.640
I do.

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:49.100
And do you, Leela, who deserves better,

00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:52.060
take Fry to be...
and I mean a lot better...

00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:53.060
to be your husband?

00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:54.850
I do.

00:21:56.690 --> 00:22:00.570
If anyone knows any reason
why these two should not be wedded...

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:02.780
doesn't have to be a good reason...

00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:04.490
Bender One-Hand?
- Nah.

00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:06.530
If two of the three of us
have to get married,

00:22:06.530 --> 00:22:08.070
I'm glad it's them.

00:22:08.070 --> 00:22:11.790
Then, I now pronounce you
husband and wife.

00:22:11.790 --> 00:22:14.000
May I kiss the bride?

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:39.940
I'm blowing up enemies with friends!

00:22:39.940 --> 00:22:42.900
I still don't get
who those weird ghost ships were.

00:22:42.900 --> 00:22:44.820
Or why they were attacking us.

00:22:44.820 --> 00:22:46.200
Who knows?

00:22:46.200 --> 00:22:48.570
Ever since we went back for Fry

00:22:48.570 --> 00:22:50.780
and sank with old Bessie,

00:22:50.780 --> 00:22:54.370
this voyage has been
an incomprehensible nightmare,

00:22:54.370 --> 00:22:59.170
drifting aimlessly in the sea
of all possible timelines.

00:22:59.170 --> 00:23:00.790
Ooh, I like this one.

00:23:00.790 --> 00:23:04.000
But this ship wasn't ready to go just yet.

00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:05.960
She was made of strong stuff,

00:23:05.960 --> 00:23:08.930
and her wires were all the right lengths.

00:23:08.930 --> 00:23:12.680
Before long, we had her patched up
and good as old.

00:23:14.680 --> 00:23:16.100
I wanna thank you all.

00:23:16.100 --> 00:23:19.440
I would've died if you hadn't risked
your lives and come back for me.

00:23:19.440 --> 00:23:22.480
We were lucky.
It could've all turned out differently.

00:23:22.480 --> 00:23:25.070
I was having some crazy visions.

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:27.860
Memories of things
I can't possibly remember.

00:23:27.860 --> 00:23:29.360
Like what?

00:23:31.820 --> 00:23:33.620
Well, like this.

00:23:34.660 --> 00:23:37.040
Whoa! We look awful

00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:39.040
but happy.

00:23:39.040 --> 00:23:40.620
What does it mean?

00:23:40.620 --> 00:23:42.500
I don't know.

00:23:42.500 --> 00:23:43.710
Let's find out.

00:23:43.710 --> 00:23:47.340
I was born to rock the boat

00:23:47.970 --> 00:23:51.590
Some may sink, but we will float

00:23:52.220 --> 00:23:57.430
Grab your coat, let's get out of here

00:24:00.560 --> 00:24:05.190
You're my witness, I'm your mutineer

00:24:08.900 --> 00:24:13.120
Long ago, we laughed at shadows

00:24:13.120 --> 00:24:16.870
Lightning flashed, thunder followed

00:24:17.950 --> 00:24:23.330
They can never find us here

00:24:25.750 --> 00:24:30.840
You're my witness,
I'm your mutineer...